{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382130-razor-claws-gift","id":1382130,"title":"razor claws gift","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-17T05:32:57-07:00","id":1382130,"title":"razor claws gift","content":"The text says ;<br /> Rank 1 Ahroun Gift / Rank 1 Get of Fenris Gift <br /> By raking his claws over stone, steel, or another hard surface, the Ahroun hones them to razor sharpness. Either a cat- or bear-spirit teaches this Gift.<br /> <br /> System: The player spends on Rage point, and the Ahroun takes a full turn sharpening her claws. All claw attacks do two additional dice of damage and are made at -1 difficulty for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> The -1 difficulty is to damage or attack <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/429-magius","name":"magius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar429_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T05:34:49-07:00","id":1382131,"title":"","content":"To attack not damage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T13:57:40-07:00","id":1382236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382130-razor-claws-gift#post1382130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All claw attacks do two additional dice of damage and are made at -1 difficulty for the rest of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand on Dwight's answer:<br /> <br /> &quot;All claw attacks (...) are made at -1difficulty for the rest of the scene.&quot; is how to parse that with the and in there.<br /> <br /> Also, in the future, it's probably best to quote from the book itself, rather than a website. The &quot;Rank 1 Ahroun Gift / Rank 1 Get of Fenris Gift&quot; format is a dead giveaway you're not directly citing the text because the books never use that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T18:22:07-07:00","id":1382651,"title":"","content":"As an aside, Razor claws was <i>not </i>that baller in Revised (it used to just be +1 damage). Frankly, I think it's insanely better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T21:51:36-07:00","id":1382679,"title":"","content":"It's a major improvement over previous editions. Razor Claw attacks are actually better than attacking with a bite in Hispo now.<br /> <br /> There's still contention over the cost though as a Rage point and a full round action makes it a huge gamble to use in sudden combat. If the design goal is to make it a risk because of the time to activate it, then the Rage cost feels excessive. If the design goal is to just give you a reason to not always activate it at the start of a fight, being a full round action is unnecessary. Having it be an instant action so you can use it with multiple actions is plenty of drawback.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T09:05:27-07:00","id":1383379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382130-razor-claws-gift?p=1382679#post1382679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's still contention over the cost though as a Rage point and a full round action makes it a huge gamble to use in sudden combat. If the design goal is to make it a risk because of the time to activate it, then the Rage cost feels excessive. If the design goal is to just give you a reason to not always activate it at the start of a fight, being a full round action is unnecessary. Having it be an instant action so you can use it with multiple actions is plenty of drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div>That it takes a full round to activate makes sense to me though; you're supposed to be scraping your claws against some kind of surface to sharpen them (<i>furiously</i> lol). Setting aside for a moment balance/value questions about the action economy, I don't think 3-6 seconds to do the sharpening is asking <i>too</i> much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T18:49:44-07:00","id":1383492,"title":"","content":"The idea of sharpening your claws taking a full round makes sense, but it's completely arbitrary that you need to physically sharpen them in that fashion. If the Gift was described as, &quot;The Garou imbues their claws with their righteous fury, causing them to become sharper and deadlier than usual.&quot; It wouldn't make sense for it to have the action needed.<br /> <br /> Brushing aside the balance/value action economy part is also pretty much dismissing the point of the contention. The most common way for a combat Gift to get saddled with a tough choice is to make it Gnosis based (since you can't use it and Rage on the same turn). It's easy to say it's not asking too much when you're setting aside things like, &quot;you might have to eat a round of being attacked because you can't defend yourself, and might potentially die before the Gift can matter.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T10:59:45-07:00","id":1384221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382130-razor-claws-gift?p=1383492#post1383492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of sharpening your claws taking a full round makes sense, but it's completely arbitrary that you need to physically sharpen them in that fashion. If the Gift was described as, &quot;The Garou imbues their claws with their righteous fury, causing them to become sharper and deadlier than usual.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Every power divorced of the narrative materials that explain their bases are arbitrary; whether they worked forward to the narrative description from a desire for it to take a turn to activate, or the other way around, I cannot say; but buying this power is a no-brainer for me: despite taking a turn to activate, it's Rank 1 (so <i>max </i>5 XP if out of breed/tribe auspice, and probably isn't a mission to obtain), its cost is low (1 of the most easily replenished resource of the 3 Garou have), and in exchange increases damage by 2 and lowers attack by 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382130-razor-claws-gift?p=1383492#post1383492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brushing aside the balance/value action economy part is also pretty much dismissing the point of the contention. The most common way for a combat Gift to get saddled with a tough choice is to make it Gnosis based (since you can't use it and Rage on the same turn). It's easy to say it's not asking too much when you're setting aside things like, &quot;you might have to eat a round of being attacked because you can't defend yourself, and might potentially die before the Gift can matter.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree that taking a full-round action <i>with</i> what amounts to somatic component makes the Gift not reasonably employable in many situations (where the Gift user is being ambushed obviously), however, I'm also okay with there being gifts that are made in such a way that they're only truly viable if someone anticipates combat. I would not have bothered to buy this Gift prior to the W20 version unless I were really and truly out of stuff to buy, and just had the XP &quot;burning a hole in my pocket&quot;.<br /> <br /> Having said that, the rule in Revised is &quot;The player spends one Rage point, and the Ahroun must take a full turn to sharpen her claws[,]&quot; and W20 is, &quot;[t]he player spends one Rage point and the Ahroun takes a full turn sharpening her claws.&quot; I've never thought of this until discussing the Gift more in-depth now, but I find there's something to be said for it being a full turn rather than the entire round of combat. Given the fact that the full-turn activation is the product of the fact there's a physical action that takes a certain amount of time--a full turn--to perform (rather than being the product of some mystical rate at which the power instantiates itself (such as with Protean 2 in Vampire, wherein you spend the blood, and it takes a turn, because that's just how long it takes for the power to manifest it self), would it not be possible to spend a number of Rage points at the beginning of combat for Razor Claws and extra actions, and then use one of the later extra actions to fulfill the narrative, physical component of activating the Gift? As I understand it, from a game standpoint, every Rage action is the effective length of the non-rage (i.e., regular) turn--I'm not saying you can literally do anything on a Rage action that you could do on a regular action (because that's obviously not the case), but, certainly if the game positions this full-turn requirement as a matter of practical/physical necessity, I don't really see why you couldn't kick on the power on the front end of the combat round, and do the actual sharpening on the back end. You wouldn't benefit from the Gift<i>that round</i>, but you also wouldn't necessarily be helpless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T12:33:19-07:00","id":1384242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382130-razor-claws-gift?p=1384221#post1384221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Every power divorced of the narrative materials that explain their bases are arbitrary;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is either kinda my point (the full-turn of sharpening is arbitrary), or fairly circular in reasoning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but buying this power is a no-brainer for me: despite taking a turn to activate, it's Rank 1 (so <i>max </i>5 XP if out of breed/tribe auspice, and probably isn't a mission to obtain), its cost is low (1 of the most easily replenished resource of the 3 Garou have), and in exchange increases damage by 2 and lowers attack by 1. </div> </div> </div>While Rage is the easiest resource to regain (remember I'm not saying activating this should be reflexive and free, just that the total costs are a bit high for what it does), it's not unlimited and people seem to get fairly liberal with giving it out beyond the ease of regaining it as is. Esp. for lower Rage characters (and the cost of raising your WP and Gnosis up to mitigate high Rage), spending Rage is still resource management. Is that bonus really worth one less extra action that fight? Or a different Gift that might be more useful?<br /> <br /> Razor Claws has also always had to contend with the Hispo form all Garou get automatically. Hispo gives a +1 damage to bites, which are already -1 difficulty compared to claws, and +1 Dexterity over Crinos, letting it capitalize on that lower difficulty attack even more. 5 XP for what amounts to between +2 and +3 damage dice (and that's with W20's buffing Razor Claws and normal claw attacks), and a lower hit rate compared to a free power you have that don't cost a full turn to activate is less of a no brainer in its wider context.<br /> <br /> Or for the more weapon Fetish happy Garou, there's the consideration of activating Razor Claws, or activating a weapon Fetish (esp. since the Garou are fans of daggers which might not have high damage but do have inherent low difficulty to attack).<br /> <br /> So there's some serious competition from tactics where that XP would be wasted because other modes of attack are the focus. Though bitey Garou have an odd curve since bite enhancing Gifts, which tend to be really good, are also high level, where there's a lot more low level claw boosters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've never thought of this until discussing the Gift more in-depth now, but I find there's something to be said for it being a full turn rather than the entire round of combat. </div> </div> </div>The two are effectively interchangeable. A full-turn action uses up your character's entire turn, including being unable to use Rage for extra actions, for the combat round. Something that takes your full turn means it's the only non-reflexively thing you can do that round. Though W20 doesn't really explain this well, and the only time it really specifies this is in an odd place (reloading firearms), but in previous editions/FAQs/etc. that's always been how the &quot;full-turn&quot; requirement has been stated to mean.<br /> <br /> So you can't activate Razor Claws and spend more Rage for extra actions, or put Razor Claws into a Rage action.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T14:24:53-07:00","id":1384265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382130-razor-claws-gift?p=1384242#post1384242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 XP for what amounts to between +2 and +3 damage dice (and that's with W20's buffing Razor Claws and normal claw attacks), and a lower hit rate compared to a free power you have that don't cost a full turn to activate is less of a no brainer in its wider context.</div> </div> </div> </div> Keep in mind also that for the Garou who have it in tribe/auspice, it's only 3 XP. Not sure how that affects your analysis, but it is a 40% reduction in cost. That's really something if you ask me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382130-razor-claws-gift?p=1384242#post1384242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or for the more weapon Fetish happy Garou, there's the consideration of activating Razor Claws, or activating a weapon Fetish (esp. since the Garou are fans of daggers which might not have high damage but do have inherent low difficulty to attack).</div> </div> </div> </div> Presumably, this group will spend the points to start the game with a magic weapon to build a combat spec around, so they may not look Razor claws for by dint of it being a power that only benefits claw attacks, and if they're to fight unarmed, they're just going to default to Hispo like you said (because it's free), and save their points for powers that will make their weapon attacks better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382130-razor-claws-gift?p=1384242#post1384242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two are effectively interchangeable. A full-turn action uses up your character's entire turn, including being unable to use Rage for extra actions, for the combat round. Something that takes your full turn means it's the only non-reflexively thing you can do that round. Though W20 doesn't really explain this well, and the only time it really specifies this is in an odd place (reloading firearms), but in previous editions/FAQs/etc. that's always been how the &quot;full-turn&quot; requirement has been stated to mean.<br /> <br /> So you can't activate Razor Claws and spend more Rage for extra actions, or put Razor Claws into a Rage action.</div> </div> </div> </div> First, I basically agree with you about the intent of the text as written, however, that's only because that interpretation is (I said above) the way I always thought the power worked until I took a really close look at it today. Having said that, even if it's <i>my </i>kneejerk (and historical) interpretation, I don't know that I can make a textual argument for it being inarguably the correct reading. I can't speak to &quot;prior editions, FAQ's, etc.&quot;, because I don't necessarily know where I'd be looking for this besides core books, but Revised is basically as poorly written in this respect as W20 (as I get to below).<br /> <br /> Re-reading the most basic parts of the systems and drama rules (i.e., this is a turn, this is action, etc.) in any of these books for the first time in years, I have to agree that W20's is written <i>extremely </i>poorly--imprecision and sloppy drafting abound. Where the book explains the action economy, and describes &quot;Multiple Actions&quot;, There is no mention of anything called a &quot;round&quot;, but then there are several mentions of &quot;Rounds&quot; (i.e., things that either take, expire, or last for, &quot;a round&quot;) in other parts of the books, and particularly in the descriptions of the mechanical operations of various Gifts. They use &quot;Turn&quot; to not only mean the discrete allotment of time a character has to act during combat pursuant to the initiative order, but <u>also</u> use the word &quot;turn&quot; the way I would use the word &quot;round&quot;, such as when the books says, &quot;[f]or each point of Rage spent, the character gets to take an additional action that turn.&quot; By using the word in seemingly two different ways, often in the same, or back-to-back sentences, they're basically creating boundless potential for ambiguities.<br /> <br /> However, with specific regard to what W20 says about the rules for reloading, I think there's something fundamentally distinguishable about the reasons provided by the book as to why you can't reload a revolver on rage actions, and the act of sharpening claws against a surface.<br /> <br /> W20 provides as follows:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Revolvers can be tricky to reload. A character with a speedloader can slap a new \u201cclip\u201d into his gun, as above. If he doesn\u2019t have a speedloader ready, he needs to take a full turn to reload that pistol manually. No other actions are possible that turn, not even when spending Rage \u2014 the gun and bullets can\u2019t move any faster. A character with a Firearms rating of 1 or better can reload without making a roll under normal circumstances, although certain complications (badly hurt, in a moving car, etc.) might demand a Dexterity + Firearms roll. Reloading a clip or speedloader with fresh bullets, however, requires a Dexterity + Fireaarms roll (difficulty 6) and an entire turn. (Again, extra Rage actions cannot speed this reloading time.) </div> </div> </div><i>W20</i>, p.297(pdf)<br /> <br /> So the reason they cite for not being able to load a revolver on Rage actions is that (unlike with Time dilation in Mage) the Werewolf is physically moving faster, but the gun and bullets cannot. Mind you, I don't understand why it is that a semi-automatic's upper receiver and magazine <i>can</i> move faster, or that a speedloader and a revolver can also move faster, but individual bullets and a revolver cannot, or why you wouldn't be able to just load single single bullet into a single chamber in the cylinder per rage action--but <i>whatever</i>; it is what it is. I digress--sharpening claws should probably not be bound by the same limitations: the claws are part of the werewolf, so they necessarily moves as fast as the Garou; and the surface upon which the claws are sharpened doesn't actually move at all, so I don't think that's a consideration either.<br /> <br /> If I had to head-canon this so that it makes <i>some </i>sort of sense in the narrative, I would posit that it's less about making sure the claws are made sharper (though that's part of it), than it is a part of some per-use chiminage or similar obeisance that must be made as part of the initial spirit pact--yes, the user needs to sharpen their claws against some surface to get them to that razor's edge, but the fact that they're taking no other action that round is spiritually important to the activation of the power, rather than an incidental byproduct of the claw sharpening process (as if you there's something about physics or material science that would prevent the werewolf from sharpening their claws as fast as they can rake their claws against whatever surface).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T16:25:03-07:00","id":1384296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382130-razor-claws-gift?p=1384265#post1384265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Keep in mind also that for the Garou who have it in tribe/auspice, it's only 3 XP. Not sure how that affects your analysis, but it is a 40% reduction in cost. That's really something if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in splat for Ahrouns and Fenrir... so while 3 XP is certainly something they're more likely to drop for it than everyone else (and that's a lot of someone else possibilities), there's still things like Breed (since Homids get item boosting Gifts that can make weapon based fighting better, while Metis and Lupus have some great bite Gifts later in their lists).<br /> <br /> I'm not saying Razor Claws is bad, it used to be bad, but that the drawbacks that have been kept while the bonuses were buffed are still a bit higher than they seem like they should be for what the Gift does, to the extent that many players/characters, even in-splat, might skip it (esp. since it doesn't work well as a back-up mid-combat if you get disarmed or something).<br /> <br /> If I'm playing a Silver Fang Ahroun that likes melee Fetishes (because Silver Fangs are noted for liking blades and getting their hands on Klaives and all that), I could grab Razor Claws... or I could pick any of the other solid Ahroun Gifts, and save the 3 XP for half of Hand Blade, which doesn't have any time restrictions, and works in Homid/Glabro, so I can rely on it instantly even in situations where I can't' carry around a bit sword or walk around in Crinos.<br /> <br /> If I'm playing an Ahroun Lupus Get of Fenris... I might skip Razor Claws because once I can pick up Gnaw and Clenched Jaw, (and maybe Rattler's Bite out of splat) I'd never use Razor Claws again, then eventually Fenris' Bite on top of all that. Yes, I know, those are all high ranked Gifts, but I have no idea why the game puts bite Gifts so far up there, or why Gnaw is as high as it is (besides perhaps needing to be two different Gifts). I'd also have Catfeet as in-splat to help bowl targets over and pin them down to initiate jaw locks on them as another reason to save my XP for bite Gifts instead of claw Gifts.<br /> <br /> If it didn't eat up a full turn? It would be much more appealing to non-claw primary warriors since it would be a functional backup Gift as well as the starting Gift for claw primary warriors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By using the word in seemingly two different ways, often in the same, or back-to-back sentences, they're basically creating boundless potential for ambiguities. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I agree the book is that inconsistent with how it uses the word turn. It never defines the word round and then uses it (which is a problem in many places). The wording by virtue of never defining rounds gets really clunky because the book does generally avoid using &quot;turn&quot; to described everyone's actions for one cycle of initiative, but not have a term for one cycle of initiative (though clearly round is meant to mean this when round is used in a timing sense) gets messy. Turn is still used consistently to mean &quot;one character's actions for that cycle of initiative,&quot; even if they don't happen at the same time in resolution; such as Rage actions happening after normal actions, but still counting as part of your turn like any other multiple action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the reason they cite for not being able to load a revolver on Rage actions is that (unlike with Time dilation in Mage) the Werewolf is physically moving faster, but the gun and bullets cannot. </div> </div> </div>Still, it's the only time where the book actually explains the implications of a full-turn action, and there's no contradictory statement in the text. All the times it's used (generally Gifts) there's the same implication of the Garou being unable to speed things up.<br /> <br /> Even so I completely agree that there's no reason reloading a revolver manually can't handle the speeds of a Garou, or even a skilled human, trying to reload it fast enough they can still do other actions. Expert speed shooters using a speedloader can get a revolver going fast enough to empty, reload, and empty again a revolver in the time the game uses for combat turns. There are manual speed loading techniques that take about twice as long as speedloaders (but are very hard to do in combat in comparison), which is still enough time to at least empty and reload in one turn. The bullets move as far as your hands can move, and the cylinder can revolve as fast as your hands can move it... doing it fast enough to damage the weapon would be...well dependent on the manufacturing but something rather insane even with supernatural powers making go super fast.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}